<%# locals: (name:, value:, checked:, id:, data: nil) %>
<%# One checkbox in a list of them, posting into an array parameter. The whole
    row is the label, so the 36px tap target is the hit area -- a min-height on
    a bare div is not clickable. select-none so a row tapped twice on a phone
    toggles twice instead of selecting its own label text, and
    break-inside-avoid so a list set in CSS columns, as Shift Coverage's is,
    never splits a row across two of them. text-base is the size
    AppFormBuilder gives its own checkbox and radio labels; unclassed, the
    text would take the browser's 16px. Unlike common/checkbox_tile it has no
    border, and it renders the checkbox itself.

    Rendered with `render layout:`: the caller's block is the label text. The
    <span> keeps it one flex item, so the flex gap never splits a title from
    its note. data: goes on the checkbox, for a Stimulus picker's hooks. %>
<label for="<%= id %>" class="flex items-center gap-2 min-h-9 px-1 cursor-pointer select-none text-base text-body break-inside-avoid">
  <%= check_box_tag name, value, checked, id:, class: AppFormBuilder::CHECKBOX_CLASSES, data: %>
  <span><%= yield %></span>
</label>
